  (d) growth at the committed Omega_m = 0.3157: D(z=0)/a = 0.788 relative to Einstein-de Sitter (Lambda SUPPRESSES late growth by 21%);
      f(z=0) = dlnD/dlna = 0.528 vs Omega_m^0.55 = 0.530 (exponent from memory, unverified); CFG176: a w = -1 or compacted
      DE-like medium has rho + 3p < 0 and repels. In standard cosmology dark energy opposes clustering; it does not drive it.
  [PASS] C14 CONTROL: the growth solver returns Einstein-de Sitter exactly at Omega_m = 1 (D = a, f = 1)
         D/a 1.00000000, f 1.00000000
  [PASS] C15 CONTROL: CFG171 / CFG176 committed numbers reproduce the door-11 record (16-205x; 0.078 vs 0.293)
         15.8-205.0; 0.0781 vs 0.293
  T5 scoring: (i) -- (a) a sweep needs a sink -> REDUCES TO 11A (G3 FAIL, 16-205x); (b) cap 0.078 vs 0.293; (c) UNDEFINED (no
      velocity model; phase 2 must price it against gate 3.03). (iii) -- NOT IMPLEMENTED (no sweeping; clustering is B's).

