VERDICT
==============================================================================================================
  (i)   a single cosmic front meets the CMB epoch only if it is initial data or superluminal (>= 99c), and then only if it
        leaves a clustering density: it REDUCES TO candidate B's cold component. A luminal front covers 1.0% of the
        last-scattering sphere by recombination (T1 and T2 FAIL). The act of compacting is 11B''s class (no-go).
        Declared primary front: T1 FAIL.
  (ii)  identical to (iii-a) or (iii-b) depending on what 'formation' means; its own content (epoch dependence) is NON-DIAGNOSTIC.
  (iii) primary (iii-a) first decoupling: H2 PASS, G5 PASS; H1 PARTIAL (bookkeeping, not a mechanism); H3 FAILS or restates B; H4 NON-DIAGNOSTIC.
        (iii-b) 'a pass at any collapse' fails the tidal dwarfs and Cassini and loses Arm C.
  Nothing here supplies B's missing mechanism. At most (iii-a) names the ownership label's assignment rule (first decoupling
  from the Hubble flow), which CFG48 G3 already scored. kappa = 1/2 FITTED; the mass is still required; nothing is closed.

